From 2ab73c6f3b919f9002d349708c5e051aa11e3316 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 00:33:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Veltro fixes: real email bodies, reply-state detection, Gmail
 reply link, Pro checkout fix
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Rebased onto current main (which already carries the earlier UI changes).
Everything here is on top of that.
Data correctness:
- gmail/route.ts: dedupe by thread, then check who sent the thread's true
  latest message. If the user already replied, the thread is excluded — it's
  handled. Fetch full message bodies (format=full) instead of metadata-only
  and extract plain text from nested multipart payloads, so the AI reads the
  actual email rather than a ~200-char snippet. awaitingReply is now a
  deterministic fact, not an LLM guess.
- analyze/route.ts: cap concurrent OpenAI calls (was unbounded Promise.all,
  up to 100 simultaneous requests on a Pro inbox); risk scoring grounded in
  real elapsed time; awaitingReply no longer inferred.
- page.tsx: feed the AI full body + real "received N hours/days ago"; the
  NO REPLY badge shows actual elapsed time instead of a hardcoded "48H".
Trust / scope:
- OAuth scope reduced to gmail.readonly. The app requested gmail.send and
  gmail.modify but never used them, while the landing page, warning modal
  and privacy policy all promise read-only access. Removed the unreachable
  /api/gmail/send endpoint and unused lib/firebase.ts.
Reply flow:
- The Gmail link opened the thread view, so users still had to find the
  sender and hit Reply. Both entry points now open Gmail's compose deep
  link with the recipient prefilled.
Billing:
- The Upgrade button linked to a static checkout with no tie to the
  signed-in account, and the webhook trusted whatever email the customer
  typed. A customer paying with a different email than they signed in with
  would never get Pro unlocked. Checkout now carries the account email as
  custom_data and the webhook reads that first.
Hardening:
- notify/route.ts: cron secret now compared with crypto.timingSafeEqual.
- track/route.ts: public tracking endpoint now allowlists event types and
  validates/caps the payload.
Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
